00:04:15,652 --> 00:04:21,652
Somewhere inside all of us is the power to change the world.

2
00:08:31,304 --> 00:08:37,304
Matilda is a comedy, family, fantasy film directed by Danny DeVito.

3
00:12:46,956 --> 00:12:52,956
Matilda Wormwood is an exquisite and intelligent little girl.

4
00:17:02,608 --> 00:17:08,608
Unfortunately, her parents, Harry and Zinnia misunderstand
her because they think she is so different.

5
00:21:18,260 --> 00:21:24,260
As time passes, she finally starts school and has a kind
teacher, loyal friends, and a sadistic headmistress.

6
00:25:33,913 --> 00:25:39,913
As she gets fed up with the constant cruelty, she begins to
realize that she has a gift of telekinetic powers.

7
00:29:49,565 --> 00:29:55,565
After some days of practice, she suddenly turns the tables to stand
up to Harry and Zinnia and outwit the headmistress.

8
00:34:05,217 --> 00:34:11,217
Matilda Wormwood, played by Mara Wilson.

9
00:38:20,869 --> 00:38:26,869
Harry Wormwood / Narrator (voice), played by Danny DeVito.

10
00:42:36,521 --> 00:42:42,521
Zinnia Wormwood, played by Rhea Perlman.

11
00:46:52,173 --> 00:46:58,173
Miss Honey, played by Embeth Davidtz.

12
00:51:07,826 --> 00:51:13,826
Agatha Trunchbull, played by Pam Ferris.

13
00:55:23,478 --> 00:55:29,478
FBI Agent, played by Paul Reubens.

14
00:59:39,130 --> 00:59:45,130
Matilda is a 1996 American fantasy comedy film co-produced and directed by Danny DeVito from a
screenplay by Nicholas Kazan and Robin Swicord, based on the 1988 novel by Roald Dahl.

15
01:03:54,782 --> 01:04:00,782
The film stars Mara Wilson as the title character, with DeVito himself (who also served in a dual role as the
narrator and Harry Wormwood), Rhea Perlman, Embeth Davidtz, and Pam Ferris in supporting roles.

16
01:08:10,434 --> 01:08:16,434
The plot centers on the titular child prodigy who develops psychokinetic abilities and uses them
to deal with her disreputable family and the tyrannical principal of her school.

17
01:12:26,086 --> 01:12:32,086
Matilda was released in the United States on August 2, 1996, by Sony
Pictures Releasing under their TriStar Pictures label.

18
01:16:41,739 --> 01:16:47,739
The film received positive reviews from critics, with praise being directed
towards its faithfulness to the novel and DeVito's direction.

19
01:20:57,391 --> 01:21:03,391
Despite this, the film was a box office disappointment,
grossing $47 million on a $36 million budget.

20
01:25:13,043 --> 01:25:19,043
However, Matilda subsequently attained greater
popularity after being released on home video.

21
01:29:28,695 --> 01:29:34,695
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, parent child
relationship, classroom, difficult childhood, child prodigy.

22
01:33:44,347 --> 01:33:50,347
The tone is lighthearted.
